# === Project-specific ===
# configs/real/ and configs/synthetic/ are INTENTIONALLY NOT ignored: Phase 5's own
# load_config_corpus.py, and Phase 6/7 (split + model training) after it, need the actual
# config text on disk, not just the DB metadata rows. 1,098 short sanitized/synthetic config
# files is small enough to commit directly — this is a hackathon repo meant to be
# clone-and-run by teammates and judges, not a data-lake-backed production system.
# If the corpus later grows much larger or picks up anything sensitive, switch to Git LFS
# or an external store instead of ignoring it outright.

# Generated PDF compliance reports (Phase 4/11 output, not source)
reports/*.pdf
output/*.pdf

